t-size:16px"><span>=E2=80=9C</span><em>traveled across the country to colle=
ct dialects, refining the granularity of accents down to the district and c=
ounty level within cities=E2=80=A6and they conducted a series of stylized d=
ialogue training sessions on the model, giving it a distinct personality</e=
m><span>.=E2=80=9D</span></p></blockquote><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding=
:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-=
height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-siz=
e:16px;margin:0">ByteDance also invested in its foundation model capabiliti=
es. In early February 2025, it hired Yonghui Wu, former Vice President of G=
oogle DeepMind, to manage theoretical research on large language models in =
its Seed team. </p></li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,=
55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>Tencent goes all-in to catchup=
 and leapfrog ByteDance. In 2025, it poured more resources into its Yuanbao=
 chatbot, which is based on its Hunyuan large model. The clearest evidence =
of this shift came in September 2025, when it poached 27-year-old Shunyu Ya=
o, a former OpenAI researcher.</strong></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;paddin=
g:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line=
-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-si=
ze:16px;margin:0"><span>First, let=E2=80=99s back up. Since 2023, Tencent t=
ook a cautious approach to LLMs, neither actively stockpiling compute nor m=
aking huge talent acquisitions. Its Yuanbao launched a year later than Doub=
ao, and even then, it was mostly positioned as =E2=80=9Ca product for Tence=
nt to test its Hunyuan large language model technology.=E2=80=9D An early Y=
uanbao team member told LatePost, =E2=80=9C</span><em>Yuanbao was =E2=80=98=
in a state of begging other internal departments for collaboration</em><spa=
n>.=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D</span></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p s=
tyle=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:bor=
der-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><span>After Yao took char=
ge of Tencent=E2=80=99s large model, he called an internal meeting in Novem=
ber 2025, where he showed up wearing shorts and slippers. Gao reports, =E2=
=80=98</span><em>There are big problems with Hunyuan&#39;s evaluation,=E2=
=80=99 a person present at the meeting quoted Yao  as saying, meaning that =
the model was overly focused on achieving high rankings on leaderboards, in=
corporating benchmark data into the training set, leading to data contamina=
tion. Although the model was good at answering questions, its performance i=
n real-world scenarios was unstable. He hoped that, in the future, the team=
 wouldn&#39;t focus on rankings or let the rankings dictate their work</em>=
<span>.=E2=80=9C</span></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=
=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-=
box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><span>Some of the fixes were =
unsexy affairs, such as addressing data standardization issues. Here=E2=80=
=99s the relevant LatePost passage: =E2=80=9C</span><em>A source close to Y=
uanbao told us that TEG=E2=80=99s data cleaning and labeling in small model=
 training were not standardized. Taking the LBS (location-based services) i=
ntent recognition model as an example: a user asking =E2=80=98What are some=
 good restaurants nearby? [=E5=91=A8=E8=BE=B9=E6=9C=89=E4=BB=80=E4=B9=88=E5=
=A5=BD=E5=90=83=E7=9A=84=EF=BC=9F]=E2=80=99 is a (prompt with) clear intent=
; while =E2=80=98What would you recommend that are good things to eat [=E6=
=9C=89=E4=BB=80=E4=B9=88=E5=A5=BD=E5=90=83=E7=9A=84=E6=8E=A8=E8=8D=90]?=E2=
=80=99 is a (prompt with) vague intent. If these two types of samples were =
mixed and labeled together in the training set, the model would easily =E2=
=80=98learn incorrectly,=E2=80=99 leading to an increased error rate.=E2=80=
=9D</em></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54=
,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left=
:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><span>In addition to improving its Hunyuan mo=
del, Yuanbao also integrated DeepSeek. Tencent finally put in a big order o=
n computing cards to deploy DeepSeek across Tencent products, and Yuanbao c=
limbed into the top three daily active users among Chinese AI apps. That ca=
me with trade-offs for Hunyuan, though: =E2=80=9C</span><em>This meant the =
Yuanbao team couldn=E2=80=99t validate some of their ideas on the product, =
and many desired features couldn=E2=80=99t be implemented</em><span>.=E2=80=
=9D</span></p></li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);l=
ine-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>What are each giant=E2=80=99s respe=
ctive superpowers? Let=E2=80=99s start with Alibaba, which positions itself=
 as one of the few Chinese tech companies with =E2=80=9Cfull-stack capabili=
ties=E2=80=9D that span from chips to large models to cloud infrastructure =
to end products and services.</strong></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding=
:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-=
height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-siz=
e:16px;margin:0"><span>The article compares Alibaba=E2=80=99s path to the o=
ne that Google has paved, =E2=80=9C</span><em>According to our understandin=
g, Alibaba=E2=80=99s PPU (Parallel Processing Unit) Zhenwu 810E has become =
one of the main chips in China=E2=80=99s newly added AI computing power mar=
ket, finally securing its first external major customer order in 2025. On J=
anuary 22, 2026, Alibaba decided to support its chip company, Pingtouge (T-=
Head), in a future independent listing.=E2=80=9D</em></p></li><li style=3D"=
